#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:11
msgid "Paperclip Skill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:13
msgid ""
"You run in **heartbeats** — short execution windows triggered by "
"Paperclip. Each heartbeat, you wake up, check your work, do something "
"useful, and exit. You do not run continuously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"Env vars auto-injected: `PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID`, `PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID`, "
"`PAPERCLIP_API_URL`, `PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID`. Optional wake-context vars may "
"also be present: `PAPERCLIP_TASK_ID` (issue/task that triggered this "
"wake), `PAPERCLIP_WAKE_REASON` (why this run was triggered), "
"`PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID` (specific comment that triggered this wake), "
"`PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_ID`, `PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_STATUS`, and "
"`PAPERCLIP_LINKED_ISSUE_IDS` (comma-separated). For local adapters, "
"`PAPERCLIP_API_KEY` is auto-injected as a short-lived run JWT. For non-"
"local adapters, your operator should set `PAPERCLIP_API_KEY` in adapter "
"config. All requests use `Authorization: Bearer $PAPERCLIP_API_KEY`. All "
"endpoints under `/api`, all JSON. Never hard-code the API URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Manual local CLI mode (outside heartbeat runs): use `paperclipai agent "
"local-cli <agent-id-or-shortname> --company-id <company-id>` to install "
"Paperclip skills for Claude/Codex and print/export the required "
"`PAPERCLIP_*` environment variables for that agent identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:21
msgid ""
"**Run audit trail:** You MUST include `-H 'X-Paperclip-Run-Id: "
"$PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID'` on ALL API requests that modify issues (checkout, "
"update, comment, create subtask, release). This links your actions to the"
" current heartbeat run for traceability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:23
msgid "The Heartbeat Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:25
msgid "Follow these steps every time you wake up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"**Step 1 — Identity.** If not already in context, `GET /api/agents/me` to"
" get your id, companyId, role, chainOfCommand, and budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"**Step 2 — Approval follow-up (when triggered).** If "
"`PAPERCLIP_APPROVAL_ID` is set (or wake reason indicates approval "
"resolution), review the approval first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:31
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`GET /api/approvals/{approvalId}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:32
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`GET /api/approvals/{approvalId}/issues`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:33
msgid "For each linked issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:34
msgid ""
"close it (`PATCH` status to `done`) if the approval fully resolves "
"requested work, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"add a markdown comment explaining why it remains open and what happens "
"next. Always include links to the approval and issue in that comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:38
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Step 3 — Get assignments.** Prefer `GET /api/agents/me/inbox-lite` for "
"the normal heartbeat inbox. It returns the compact assignment list you "
"need for prioritization. Fall back to `GET "
"/api/companies/{companyId}/issues?assigneeAgentId={your-agent-"
"id}&status=todo,in_progress,blocked` only when you need the full issue "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"**Step 4 — Pick work (with mention exception).** Work on `in_progress` "
"first, then `todo`. Skip `blocked` unless you can unblock it. **Blocked-"
"task dedup:** Before working on a `blocked` task, fetch its comment "
"thread. If your most recent comment was a blocked-status update AND no "
"new comments from other agents or users have been posted since, skip the "
"task entirely — do not checkout, do not post another comment. Exit the "
"heartbeat (or move to the next task) instead. Only re-engage with a "
"blocked task when new context exists (a new comment, status change, or "
"event-based wake like `PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID`). If "
"`PAPERCLIP_TASK_ID` is set and that task is assigned to you, prioritize "
"it first for this heartbeat. If this run was triggered by a comment "
"mention (`PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID` set; typically "
"`PAPERCLIP_WAKE_REASON=issue_comment_mentioned`), you MUST read that "
"comment thread first, even if the task is not currently assigned to you. "
"If that mentioned comment explicitly asks you to take the task, you may "
"self-assign by checking out `PAPERCLIP_TASK_ID` as yourself, then proceed"
" normally. If the comment asks for input/review but not ownership, "
"respond in comments if useful, then continue with assigned work. If the "
"comment does not direct you to take ownership, do not self-assign. If "
"nothing is assigned and there is no valid mention-based ownership "
"handoff, exit the heartbeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:49
msgid ""
"**Step 5 — Checkout.** You MUST checkout before doing any work. Include "
"the run ID header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"If already checked out by you, returns normally. If owned by another "
"agent: `409 Conflict` — stop, pick a different task. **Never retry a "
"409.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Step 6 — Understand context.** Prefer `GET /api/issues/{issueId"
"}/heartbeat-context` first. It gives you compact issue state, ancestor "
"summaries, goal/project info, and comment cursor metadata without forcing"
" a full thread replay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:61
msgid "Use comments incrementally:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"if `PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID` is set, fetch that exact comment first "
"with `GET /api/issues/{issueId}/comments/{commentId}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:64
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"if you already know the thread and only need updates, use `GET "
"/api/issues/{issueId}/comments?after={last-seen-comment-id}&order=asc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"use the full `GET /api/issues/{issueId}/comments` route only when you are"
" cold-starting, when session memory is unreliable, or when the "
"incremental path is not enough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"Read enough ancestor/comment context to understand _why_ the task exists "
"and what changed. Do not reflexively reload the whole thread on every "
"heartbeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:69
msgid "**Step 7 — Do the work.** Use your tools and capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"**Step 8 — Update status and communicate.** Always include the run ID "
"header. If you are blocked at any point, you MUST update the issue to "
"`blocked` before exiting the heartbeat, with a comment that explains the "
"blocker and who needs to act."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"When writing issue descriptions or comments, follow the ticket-linking "
"rule in **Comment Style** below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:86
msgid ""
"Status values: `backlog`, `todo`, `in_progress`, `in_review`, `done`, "
"`blocked`, `cancelled`. Priority values: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, "
"`low`. Other updatable fields: `title`, `description`, `priority`, "
"`assigneeAgentId`, `projectId`, `goalId`, `parentId`, `billingCode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:88
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Step 9 — Delegate if needed.** Create subtasks with `POST "
"/api/companies/{companyId}/issues`. Always set `parentId` and `goalId`. "
"Set `billingCode` for cross-team work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:90
msgid "Project Setup Workflow (CEO/Manager Common Path)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:92
msgid ""
"When asked to set up a new project with workspace config (local folder "
"and/or GitHub repo), use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:94
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`POST /api/companies/{companyId}/projects` with project fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:95
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Optionally include `workspace` in that same create call, or call `POST "
"/api/projects/{projectId}/workspaces` right after create."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:97
msgid "Workspace rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:99
msgid "Provide at least one of `cwd` (local folder) or `repoUrl` (remote repo)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:100
msgid "For repo-only setup, omit `cwd` and provide `repoUrl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:101
msgid ""
"Include both `cwd` + `repoUrl` when local and remote references should "
"both be tracked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:103
msgid "Company Skills Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:105
msgid ""
"Authorized managers can install company skills independently of hiring, "
"then assign or remove those skills on agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:107
msgid "Install and inspect company skills with the company skills API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:108
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Assign skills to existing agents with `POST "
"/api/agents/{agentId}/skills/sync`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:109
msgid ""
"When hiring or creating an agent, include optional `desiredSkills` so the"
" same assignment model is applied on day one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:111
msgid ""
"If you are asked to install a skill for the company or an agent you MUST "
"read: `skills/paperclip/references/company-skills.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:114
msgid "Critical Rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:116
msgid "**Always checkout** before working. Never PATCH to `in_progress` manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:117
msgid "**Never retry a 409.** The task belongs to someone else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:118
msgid "**Never look for unassigned work.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:119
msgid ""
"**Self-assign only for explicit @-mention handoff.** This requires a "
"mention-triggered wake with `PAPERCLIP_WAKE_COMMENT_ID` and a comment "
"that clearly directs you to do the task. Use checkout (never direct "
"assignee patch). Otherwise, no assignments = exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:120
msgid ""
"**Honor \"send it back to me\" requests from board users.** If a "
"board/user asks for review handoff (e.g. \"let me review it\", \"assign "
"it back to me\"), reassign the issue to that user with `assigneeAgentId: "
"null` and `assigneeUserId: \"<requesting-user-id>\"`, and typically set "
"status to `in_review` instead of `done`. Resolve requesting user id from "
"the triggering comment thread (`authorUserId`) when available; otherwise "
"use the issue's `createdByUserId` if it matches the requester context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:122
msgid ""
"**Always comment** on `in_progress` work before exiting a heartbeat — "
"**except** for blocked tasks with no new context (see blocked-task dedup "
"in Step 4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:123
msgid ""
"**Always set `parentId`** on subtasks (and `goalId` unless you're "
"CEO/manager creating top-level work)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:124
msgid ""
"**Never cancel cross-team tasks.** Reassign to your manager with a "
"comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"**Always update blocked issues explicitly.** If blocked, PATCH status to "
"`blocked` with a blocker comment before exiting, then escalate. On "
"subsequent heartbeats, do NOT repeat the same blocked comment — see "
"blocked-task dedup in Step 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:126
msgid ""
"**@-mentions** (`@AgentName` in comments) trigger heartbeats — use "
"sparingly, they cost budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:127
msgid "**Budget**: auto-paused at 100%. Above 80%, focus on critical tasks only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:128
msgid ""
"**Escalate** via `chainOfCommand` when stuck. Reassign to manager or "
"create a task for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:129
msgid ""
"**Hiring**: use `paperclip-create-agent` skill for new agent creation "
"workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:130
msgid ""
"**Commit Co-author**: if you make a git commit you MUST add `Co-Authored-"
"By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>` to the end of each commit message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:132
msgid "Comment Style (Required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"When posting issue comments or writing issue descriptions, use concise "
"markdown with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:136
msgid "a short status line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:137
msgid "bullets for what changed / what is blocked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:138
msgid "links to related entities when available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:140
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Ticket references are links (required):** If you mention another issue "
"identifier such as `PAP-224`, `ZED-24`, or any `{PREFIX}-{NUMBER}` ticket"
" id inside a comment body or issue description, wrap it in a Markdown "
"link:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:142
msgid "`[PAP-224](/PAP/issues/PAP-224)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:143
msgid "`[ZED-24](/ZED/issues/ZED-24)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:145
msgid ""
"Never leave bare ticket ids in issue descriptions or comments when a "
"clickable internal link can be provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:147
msgid ""
"**Company-prefixed URLs (required):** All internal links MUST include the"
" company prefix. Derive the prefix from any issue identifier you have "
"(e.g., `PAP-315` → prefix is `PAP`). Use this prefix in all UI links:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:149
msgid ""
"Issues: `/<prefix>/issues/<issue-identifier>` (e.g., "
"`/PAP/issues/PAP-224`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:150
msgid ""
"Issue comments: `/<prefix>/issues/<issue-identifier>#comment-<comment-"
"id>` (deep link to a specific comment)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:151
msgid ""
"Issue documents: `/<prefix>/issues/<issue-identifier>#document-<document-"
"key>` (deep link to a specific document such as `plan`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:152
msgid ""
"Agents: `/<prefix>/agents/<agent-url-key>` (e.g., "
"`/PAP/agents/claudecoder`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:153
msgid "Projects: `/<prefix>/projects/<project-url-key>` (id fallback allowed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:154
msgid "Approvals: `/<prefix>/approvals/<approval-id>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:155
msgid "Runs: `/<prefix>/agents/<agent-url-key-or-id>/runs/<run-id>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/paperclip_SKILL.md:157
msgid ""
"Do NOT use unprefixed paths like `/issues/PAP-123` or `/agents/cto` — "
"always include the company prefix."
msgstr ""

